bench.ltpv6 - IPv6 LTP Benchmark Test
======================================

PURPOSE
-------
This test verifies dual-stack IPv6 support for LTP (udplso/udplsi) by running
benchmark tests using IPv6 loopback addresses [::1] instead of IPv4 localhost.

This is a direct adaptation of the demos/bench-ltp test, modified to use IPv6
addressing to verify the dual-stack capability added to udplso and udplsi.

TEST STRUCTURE
--------------
- 2.bench.ltpv6/  - Node 2 configuration (sender)
- 3.bench.ltpv6/  - Node 3 configuration (receiver)
- global.ionrc    - Contact plan shared by both nodes
- dotest          - Main test script
- cleanup         - Cleanup script

KEY DIFFERENCES FROM bench.ltp
-------------------------------
1. Uses IPv6 loopback address [::1] instead of localhost or 127.0.0.1
2. LTP configuration in bench.ltprc files uses:
   - Node 2: udplso [::1]:2113 and udplsi [::1]:2112
   - Node 3: udplso [::1]:2112 and udplsi [::1]:2113

RUNNING THE TEST
----------------
1. Build ION with dual-stack UDP support
2. cd tests/bench.ltpv6
3. ./dotest

The test will:
- Start two ION nodes configured for IPv6 communication
- Send bundles of various sizes between nodes
- Report throughput and completion status
- Clean up automatically

EXPECTED RESULTS
----------------
The test should complete successfully, demonstrating that:
- udplso can send to IPv6 addresses
- udplsi can bind to and receive on IPv6 addresses
- LTP segments are successfully transmitted over IPv6
- Performance is comparable to IPv4 bench.ltp test

VERIFICATION
------------
Success indicators:
- Both nodes start without errors
- Log messages show IPv6 addresses (e.g., "[::1]:2112")
- All bundles are received
- Test exits with status 0

If the test fails, check:
- IPv6 is enabled on your system
- Firewall allows IPv6 loopback traffic
- ION logs in 2.bench.ltpv6/ and 3.bench.ltpv6/ directories
